WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.500
Hey guys, it's Jan here.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.250
Ryan Reynolds has said that his Deadpool movie
has 'more Easter eggs than the Easter bunny',

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.630
so I've put together every easter egg and
reference I could find in this video.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:16.760
I'm sure you'll have spotted other cool ones
too, so do share those in the comments below.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.490
And just before I kick off, I've got an awesome
giveaway, so if you'd like a chance to win

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.929
some cool Deadpool merch, make sure you subscribe
and comment about your favourite easter egg

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:27.929
on this video.

00:00:27.929 --> 00:00:32.830
For more details and ways to enter the comp,
check out the Gleam link in the video description

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:33.830
below!

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.920
Now, a quick reminder: there will be spoilers
ahead, so if you're not ready for that, check

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.440
out my non-spoiler review of the movie here!

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.030
First up, the opening credits are littered
with some great meta movie jokes such as starring

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:50.750
"God's Perfect Idiot", "A British Villain"
"The Hot Chick", "A CGI Character" "A gratuitous

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.750
cameo" etc.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.899
And floating among the credits is a coffee
cup labelled Rob L. in honour of Deadpool

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:58.530
comic book co-creator Rob Liefeld.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:03.780
There's also a nod to Ryan Reynold's turn
as Hal Jordan in the 2011 Green Lantern movie

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.340
with a Green Lantern trading card popping
out of a wallet.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:11.731
And a copy of People Magazine floats by with
Ryan Reynolds on the cover as 2010 Sexiest

00:01:11.731 --> 00:01:17.101
Man of the Year and later in the movie, Deadpool
stuffs a stack of Hugh Jackman 2008 Sexiest

00:01:17.101 --> 00:01:19.110
Man of the Year magazines into his gun bag.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.159
And, as you'd expect, there's a ton of comic-book
references in the movie too.

00:01:23.159 --> 00:01:28.060
The humorous scene with pizza delivery guy
Jeremy and apartment owner Mr Merchant is

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.659
a subplot that closely resembles a storyline
from the comics where Deadpool was contracted

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:37.020
to kill a pizza delivery guy who'd spread
a nasty rumour about a girl in high school.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.971
In the comics the pizza guy is called Gavin
whereas in the movie Gavin is actually the

00:01:40.971 --> 00:01:43.520
first name of the guy who owns the apartment.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.450
Given this sequence involves two guys, a pizza,
and later a girl, it's also a nod to Ryan

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:53.080
Reynold's breakout role as Michael "Berg"
Bergen in the TV comedy series Two Guys, a

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.479
Girl and a Pizza Place.

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:58.939
And Deadpool's line 'What situation isn't
improved by pizza?' is another nod to the

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:02.189
situation comedy, or sitcom, that Reynolds
made his name in.

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:05.799
And did you notice that the pizza box is from
Feige's pizzeria?

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:11.400
Which is a nice allusion to Marvel Studios'
president Kevin Feige and former X-Men producer.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.740
Later when Wade meets the girl the pizza guy
was stalking, he says he should have brought

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.000
his rollerblades, which is a callback to the
comics where Deadpool goes rollerblading.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.170
Wade's mercenary bar hangout is called "Sister
Margaret's School for Wayward Children", which

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:28.130
is the same as Deadpool's mercenary hangout
in the comics, which is also known as the

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.330
Hell House.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.640
Rob Liefeld, Deadpool's co-creator, has a
small cameo as one of the patrons at Weasel's

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:38.370
bar and when Wade walks in for the first time,
you can hear the words say "Fuck Liefeld!",

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.910
which is likely an allusion to his controversial
status with some comic book fans.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.830
By the way, Deadpool's costume has the trademark
Liefeld pouches.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:51.340
And Boothe, one of the mercenaries at the
bar, could be a nod to Assassin-8, aka Andre

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.750
Booth, the cyborg killer from the comics.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.390
And the character Buck feels like it's based
on the character Steele Fitzpatrick, aka CF,

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.770
who was also a portly mercenary and friend
of Deadpool's at the Hellhouse.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:06.690
In the movie, Wade Wilson chooses the name
Deadpool from the betting pool that Weasel

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:11.530
runs on which mercenary will die next, a parallel
to the comic book origin story where Wade

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:15.310
Wilson chooses his name from a betting pool
run on which inmate would die next at the

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.250
Weapon X government experimentation facility.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:23.120
One of the other superhero names suggested
by Weasel is Scaredevil, a jibe at Daredevil

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.190
who Deadpool has teamed up with in the comics.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.840
And the action scene where Deadpool is fighting
goons in a corridor is reminiscent of a similar

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.090
scene in Marvel's Daredevil on Netflix, which
itself was a nod to a fight scene in the movie

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.090
Oldboy.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.290
And by the way, Philip Silvera was the stunt
coordinator for both Deadpool and Netflix's

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.480
Daredevil.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.530
Wade also joked he should be Captain Deadpool,
which is both a nod to Ryan Reynold's role

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:50.650
as Captain Excellent in the movie Paper Man
and probably also a crack at Captain America.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:54.980
There's also a bit of parody of Captain America's
shield when Deadpool throws a car wheel rim

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.470
at Ajax when they're on the highway.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:02.140
Talking about names, Deadpool jokes that Ajax's
name sounds 'surprisingly made-up' and that

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.910
he probably took it from a dish soap.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:09.120
He also wonders what Ajax's real name might
be and offers Bruce and Scott as possibilities,

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.290
which could be nods to the Hulk's name Bruce
Banner, and Cyclops's name Scott Summers or

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.200
Ant-Man's name Scott Lang.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.950
Ajax's obsession with not using his real name,
Francis, is taken from the Deadpool and Death

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:25.920
1998 annual in which Deadpool discovers that
Ajax hates being called by his real name.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:30.920
And in a post-Breaking Bad world, Ajax's often-repeated
line 'What's my name?'

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.500
also has a ring of Walter White's words 'Say
My Name' about it.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.890
The name tag Wade steals from Ajax has the
surname 'Freeman' on it, which is likely a

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.480
nod to Marvel comic book inker Jeremy Freeman
who inked an issue of Cable and Deadpool where

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.430
Ajax returns from the dead on Wade's TV screen.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.790
Oh, and by the way, in the comics, as in the
film, Ajax explains how his nerve endings

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.660
have been scorched so he no longer feels pain.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:58.810
And because Fox have the movie rights to Marvel's
mutant superheroes X-Men and Marvel can't

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:03.470
use the word mutant in their movies, Ajax's
description of his henchwoman Angel Dust as

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:08.510
'inhumanly strong' feels like a cheeky nod
to Marvel's Inhumans, who are part of the

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:12.070
MCU in Agents of SHIELD and their own upcoming
movie.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:16.510
When Wade gets a Voltron Defender of the Universe
ring with his arcade tickets, it's an easter

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.810
egg to the time in the comics when Deadpool
converted himself into Voltron combining his

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:23.810
supporting Brute Force characters into one
super robot.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:27.510
And there's another nod to this at the end
of the movie when Deadpool says to Colossus

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:32.140
and Negasonic Teenage Warhead, "for a minute
there it felt like we were 3 mini lion-robots

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.120
coming together to form one super-robot".

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:39.920
The movie has some nice hints to Vanessa's
Copycat alter ego in the comics, for example,

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.560
the white streaks in her dark hair hint at
Copycat's white hair.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:47.890
And because Copycat has blue skin in the comics
we sometimes see Vanessa with blue objects

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:53.090
such as her blue bedsheets and her transparent
umbrella which has a blue rim and handle.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:57.050
When Vanessa says to Wade "[Red's] your colour,
it brings out the bloodshot in your eyes",

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.880
it's a nod to Copycat's sometimes red eyes
in the comics.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.160
There's a funny Star Wars joke between Wade
and Vanessa when she tells him to 'ride a

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.260
bitch's back like Yoda does Luke's' and notes
she's referencing The Empire Strikes Back,

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.140
not the first Star Wars movie.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:15.170
And when Wade replies to her "it's like I
made you in a computer", it's a cool easter

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:19.090
egg to X-Men 2 when Mystique is searching
through Stryker's computer and Copycat's name

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.090
appears.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.770
And in the trailer Vanessa's line "I've played
a lot of roles in my life.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.840
Damsel in distress ain't one of them" is a
reference to both her shapeshifting powers

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:31.690
as Copycat in the comics and also to Morena
Baccarin's multiple TV and film roles such

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.770
as Gotham, Firefly, Serenity, V, and many
more.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:39.970
And at the strip club where Vanessa works,
Stan Lee cameos as an MC introducing the strippers

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:43.130
on stage with the line "give it up for chastity".

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.690
And we also hear Lee's voice in the background
at the club saying, "You can't buy love, but

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.430
you can rent it for 3 minutes!"

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:52.170
When Wade finds out about his cancer at the
oncologist, there's a nod to Deadpool's hatred

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:56.880
of clowns in the comics when he quips to the
doctor, "You're clowning, not clowning, I

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.880
sense clowns."

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:01.870
The Bea Arthur T-shirt Wade wears at numerous
points in the film is a call-back to the comics

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:07.380
where Deadpool is a fan of Golden Girls actress
Bea Arthur calling her the sexiest woman alive.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.990
Back at Weasel's bar, Wade's joke that the
Recruiter's proposal sounds like a dodgy infomercial

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.380
is a call-back to the comics where Deadpool
mocks supervillain Taskmaster.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:20.270
Oh, and when he calls the Recruiter Agent
Smith, it's a nice nod to the Matrix antagonist

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.610
of the same name.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:25.241
And when Wade tells the Recruiter that 'I
tried the hero ... and it left a mark', it's

00:07:25.241 --> 00:07:28.680
a dig at his role in the critically panned
Green Lantern movie.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:33.260
And earlier in the movie at the skateboard
park when Wade looks at his green-rimmed sunglasses

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:37.430
in disgust and throws them away, it feels
like a jab at the Green Lantern's mask.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:42.050
Later, at Ajax's Workshop, Ryan Reynolds pokes
yet more fun at the Green Lantern movie with

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:46.030
Wade's line "Please don't make my suit green
or animated!".

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:49.340
Also at the Workshop, we get a glimpse of
the mutant Marrow, who has bones which grow

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.470
out of her body.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:54.860
When Wade's in the glass oxygen-deprivation
case, he steals a match from Angel Dust and

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.410
lights it as a way to escape.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:00.270
It feels like a nod to Ryan Reynolds' movie
Buried where he's trapped in a coffin with

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.690
nothing but a lighter and a cellphone to help
him get out.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:08.110
And when Wade emerges from the rubble of the
workshop, it feels reminiscent of the way

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:12.560
Deadpool's hand emerges from the rubble in
the post-credits of X-Men Origins: Wolverine.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:16.460
Speaking of that movie, there's a side swipe
at that version of Deadpool when in this movie

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:21.280
the Merc with a Mouth says 'shit's just gone
sideways in the most colossal way' and the

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:25.850
camera immediately cuts to an action figure
of the Origins Wolverine Deadpool with its

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:30.580
mouth sewn shut, and the joke continues as
we hear Wade say 'this is my most prized possession',

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:36.150
but as the camera pans up we realise he's
actually talking about Wham!'s Make It Big

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.150
album.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.830
And there's another reference later to that
Deadpool when Ajax tells Wade to shut up or

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.760
he'll sew his pretty mouth shut.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:48.020
And also when Wade is in the oxygen-deprivation
tank and refuses to say Ajax's name, we hear

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:51.300
Deadpool's voiceover say: 'sorry, Francis,
my lips are sealed.'

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.930
By the way, when Wade jokes that he looks
like he was bitten by a radioactive Shar-Pei,

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.510
it's an easter egg to a very similar moment
in Cable &amp; Deadpool #2 which was published

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.790
in 2004 and coincidentally seemed to predict
Ryan Reynolds would play Deadpool.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.300
There's several Spider-Man references in the
film too including the line "Go get her tiger"

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.990
which Weasel says to Wade and which Deadpool
also later says to Negasonic Teenage Warhead.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:18.040
The line's an echo of Mary Jane's words to
Peter Parker "Go get 'em, tiger" at the end

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.790
of the Spider-Man 2 movie.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:24.730
And when the action freezes Deadpool mid-air,
we find him in a typical upside down Spider-Man

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.790
pose.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.200
Spider-Monkey from the alternate Marvel Apes
universe also gets a mention when Deadpool

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.750
is fighting 2 female opponents.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.470
And in Wade's final voiceover his mention
of "your friendly neighbourhood pool guy"

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.730
is an obvious play on Spider-man's popular
phrase "your friendly neighbourhood Spider-man".

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.170
There's also a street sign for Parker Boulevard.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:46.170
And a host of other streets signs are nods
to the comic books or the movie itself including

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:51.290
Fabian Road and Nicieza Street, which are
named after Deadpool co-creator Fabian Nicieza,

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:55.990
Miller Street named for director Tim Miller
or actor TJ Miller who plays Weasel, Silver

00:09:55.990 --> 00:10:00.580
Avenue and Shaham Circle which are nods to
Deadpool VFX coordinators Scott Aaron Silver

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.580
and Tamar Shaham.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:07.010
There are also loads of jokes and references
to Fox's popular mutant movie franchise, X-Men,

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:08.649
including a glimpse of the X-Jet.

00:10:08.649 --> 00:10:13.440
When Colossus says they're off to see Professor
X, Deadpool asks "McAvoy or Stewart?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.860
These timelines are so confusing".

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.230
Deadpool's joke about only ever seeing two
X-Men at the mansion and not being able to

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:23.710
afford more X-Men characters is a reference
to this R-rated movie's tight budget compared

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.680
to the budget of many PG13 superhero movies.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:31.010
And Negasonic Teenage Warhead pokes fun at
the franchise with jokes about matching unitards

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:33.380
and a house that blows up every few years.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:37.360
And Deadpool's tirade about the 'Neverland
mansion', in other words Xavier's home for

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.760
gifted youngsters, and Charles Xavier being
a "creepy Heaven's Gate-looking motherfucker"

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:46.210
is a nod to some of Professor X's less savoury
moments in the comics, for example, when he

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:49.140
admitted he was in love with the 15-year old
Jean Grey.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.270
When Colossus tells Negasonic Teenage Warhead
that breakfast is the most important meal

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:57.620
of the day and offers her a protein bar, it's
a call-back to a 'Candy Variant' cover of

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.420
Deadpool which features a fake advertisement
for a protein bar.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:05.710
Marvel issued the cover as a dig at their
rivals DC who had been running half-page Twix

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.120
ads in their comics.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.640
By the way, that cover also shows Deadpool
and Rhino fighting and there was a Rhino easter

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.070
egg in Weasel's bar with a Rhino head trophy
on one of the walls.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.990
When comic book writer Grant Morrison created
Negasonic Teenage Warhead, he named her after

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.660
a song by American rock band Monster Magnet.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:27.380
In the movie, Deadpool thinks it's the 'coolest
name ever', which is exactly what the screenwriters

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.640
thought too which is why they included her
in their script!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:34.710
In the comics, Warhead is a member of the
Hellfire Club and a student of telepath Emma

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:38.622
Frost, whereas in the movie she's an X-Men
trainee, and later at the junkyard we see

00:11:38.622 --> 00:11:40.550
her in the X-Men uniform.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:45.810
And let's not forget the reference Deadpool
makes to X-Man Hank McCoy when he asks Colossus

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.040
to tell Beast to stop shitting on his lawn.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:52.160
I just mentioned the junkyard, well, when
Deadpool arrives there, his line "time to

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.870
make the chimi-fucking-changas" is a cool
nod to the comics where he has a penchant

00:11:55.870 --> 00:12:00.510
for repeating the word "chimichanga" over
and over because he likes the way it sounds.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:04.800
As Deadpool, Warhead and Colossus stride in
to confront Ajax and his gang, the hip hop

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:09.010
song "X Gon' Give It to Ya" by DMX plays,
which is a nice nod to the Weapon X program

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.750
which created Deadpool.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.279
When Deadpool removes his underwear to use
as a white flag in the junkyard scene it's

00:12:14.279 --> 00:12:16.790
a nod to a similar moment in Deadpool #31.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:21.400
There's a great moment when Deadpool's fighting
one of Ajax's men and suddenly they stop and

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.230
the other guy is revealed as Bob who Deadpool
knows.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:28.350
This funny scene could be a nod to Bob, a
Hydra agent who has numerous storylines with

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.350
Deadpool in the comics.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.940
Or given that Deadpool mentions Jacksonville
and that the food Bob's wife makes is bad

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:37.450
for the waistline, the character could be
a reference to "Billy Bob" Reilly, who grew

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:40.810
up in Jacksonville and whose alias is Phat,
spelt P-H-A-T.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:44.770
In fact, the character Phat actually appeared
in X-Men: The Last Stand.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:49.440
And when Ajax says to Deadpool "I hear you
grow back body parts […] when I'm finished,

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.580
body parts are gonna have to grow back you",
well, it resembles the time in Cable &amp; Deadpool

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:58.760
"If Looks Could Kill" when Deadpool regenerates
after being turned into nothing but a puddle.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:02.380
And when Ajax sticks a knife in Deadpool's
head and he starts to hear Chicago's "You're

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:07.260
The Inspiration", it's a call-back to Cable
and Deadpool #49 when Ka-Zar sticks a knife

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:10.300
through Deadpool's head while a tune plays
in the background.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.480
The final showdown on what looks like a rusty
old helicarrier and the post-credits joke

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.149
about Samuel L. Jackson showing up is a poke
at Marvel's Cinematic Universe.

00:13:18.149 --> 00:13:20.640
Ok, let's talk about the fourth wall.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.570
In the comics, Deadpool famously breaks the
fourth wall and the movie certainly doesn't

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.570
disappoint.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.950
There's a moment where Colossus tells Deadpool
he can hear him talking and Deadpool replies,

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:33.110
"I wasn't talking to you, I was talking to
them", which is a nice call-back to a similar

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:37.350
moment in the comics between Deadpool, Benjamin
Franklin and SHIELD agent Emily Preston.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:41.370
There are loads more examples such as when
Deadpool flicks chewing gum on the camera

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.370
lens while in the taxi.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:46.709
Also, when he talks to the audience saying,
"Oh hello, I know right, whose balls did I

00:13:46.709 --> 00:13:49.060
have to fondle to get my own movie?!

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:53.520
Rhymes with Poolverine, and let me tell you,
he's got a nice pair of smooth criminals down

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.779
under", he adds in his best Aussie accent.

00:13:54.779 --> 00:14:00.060
Of course, there's more ribbing of Hugh Jackman
later when Wade reveals a Hugh Jackman face

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.650
cut-out and stapled to his own face to hide
his scars from Vanessa.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:07.950
And there's even a fourth wall meta joke with
Deadpool pointing out a fourth wall break

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.760
within another fourth wall, a nod to the time
when Deadpool has explained the fourth wall

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.910
to other comic characters in the comic books.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:17.959
Other fourth wall breaks include Deadpool
saying "Cue The Music" and when he freezes

00:14:17.959 --> 00:14:21.470
the action to explain why this is a different
kind of superhero movie.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:26.620
And there is an absolute barrage of pop culture
references, for example Deadpool has an Adventure

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:30.899
Time watch and a Hello Kitty duffel bag, he
jokes about Honey Boo Boo reality TV star

00:14:30.899 --> 00:14:35.670
Mama June, he argues about the merits of different
IKEA furniture with Blind Al, he has a Deadpool

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:39.450
toy on the shelf in his apartment as well
as a Star Wars lunchbox, and he pokes fun

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.180
at Batman and Robin, saying Robin loves Batman.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:45.831
And speaking of Batman, when Wade wonders
if his mask is muffling his voice, it's a

00:14:45.831 --> 00:14:49.130
little jab at Tom Hardy's Bane in The Dark
Knight Rises.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:53.471
When fellow bar patron Buck comments that
he'd 'hit this' in reference to Vanessa, she

00:14:53.471 --> 00:14:56.500
makes a Lord of the Rings reference when she
grabs his balls and tells him to 'say the

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.760
words, fat Gandalf'.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:03.390
And Wade tells Vanessa to 'Hakuna his tatas',
making a Lion King reference to the song Hakuna

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:04.390
Matata.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:08.010
Wade's promise that he'll return and boombox
Careless Whisper outside Vanessa's window

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.450
is a nod to director Cameron Crowe's first
movie Say Anything, where John Cusack plays

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.649
Peter Gabriel's In Your Eyes outside his ex-girlfriend's
window.

00:15:15.649 --> 00:15:20.450
There's several other musical jokes in the
movie including nods to nu metal band Limp

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.870
Bizkit, the rock band Spin Doctors, and, of
course, more mentions of Wham!'s second album,

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:29.100
Make It Big, which featured Careless Whisper;
and Deadpool also wears a t-shirt from the

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.300
rock musical Rent.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:35.370
Oh, and Negasonic Teenage Warhead's shaven
head leads Deadpool to tell her 'nothing compares

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:40.120
2 u' and to call her Sinead, after Irish singer
Sinead O'Connor who had a massive hit with

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:45.350
that song back in 1990, and he also calls
Warhead 'Ripley from Alien 3', after Sigourney

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:47.800
Weaver's iconic character in that movie.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:52.050
There's also a great joke about the Taken
franchise and its star Liam Neeson's parenting

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:56.130
skills; and a shout-out to The Godfather when
Deadpool turns up at the X-Mansion and tells

00:15:56.130 --> 00:16:00.170
Colossus that 'I've got an offer you can't
refuse'; and in the montage where Deadpool's

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:06.000
searching for Francis, the kill using a Zamboni
ice resurfacer is a nod to Austin Powers.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.940
Weasel suggests Wade should start making his
own horror movies as his face looks like the

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:14.250
Nightmare On Elm Street character 'Freddie
Krueger fucked a topographical map of Utah'.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:18.339
There's also a nod to the Marvel Comics' Blade
franchise when Weasel tells Ajax and Angel

00:16:18.339 --> 00:16:22.640
Dust to enjoy their Blade 2 midnight screening,
which is interesting as Ryan Reynolds has

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:27.000
said it was his role as vampire hunter Hannibal
King in Blade: Trinity which brought him to

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:31.480
the attention of a Fox executive, who thought
that character and Deadpool had many similarities

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.290
and asked him to play the role.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:38.740
The reference to Danny Boyle's movie 127 Hours
when Deadpool saws off his own hand was brilliant,

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:42.690
and just before he jumps on to the garbage
truck, he also references author Judy Blume's

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:45.540
1970 young adult novel, 'Are You There God?

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.130
It's Me, Margaret.'

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:51.850
Also when Deadpool introduces himself to taxi
driver Dopinder as "Pool, Dead" it feels like

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:56.250
a funny twist on James Bond's classic line
"Bond, James Bond", and he also tells Dopinder

00:16:56.250 --> 00:17:00.600
that director Ron Howard's sci-fi movie Cocoon
about a bunch of old people made young again

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:04.209
by an alien 'life force' is 'pure pornography'.

00:17:04.209 --> 00:17:08.470
When Deadpool and Blind Al argue about whether
looks are important or not, he asks her: 'what

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:13.370
do I keep telling you, Mrs Magoo?', a nod
to the near-sighted cartoon character Mr Magoo.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:18.079
And when Blind Al says 'looks aren't everything',
Deadpool keeps the pop-culture and meta-references

00:17:18.079 --> 00:17:22.740
flowing with his comments on footballer David
Beckham's high-pitched voice, and adds 'do

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:26.649
you think Ryan Reynolds got this far on his
superior acting method?'

00:17:26.649 --> 00:17:31.399
The various toy or animated unicorns and rainbow
jokes are a reference to the popular memes

00:17:31.399 --> 00:17:33.889
of Deadpool riding a unicorn or Pegasus.

00:17:33.889 --> 00:17:37.413
The final scene where Wade says to Colossus
"I'm just a boy about to stand in front of

00:17:37.413 --> 00:17:41.669
a girl and tell her, WTF am I going to tell
her?" is a parody of Notting Hill where Julia

00:17:41.669 --> 00:17:46.240
Roberts says to Hugh Grant "I'm also just
a girl standing in front of a boy asking him

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:47.250
to love her".

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.809
There's a whole bunch of meta-moments in the
movie, for example, right at the start Deadpool

00:17:51.809 --> 00:17:56.340
picks up a Haunted Segway Tours leaflet, looks
at it thoughtfully and then saves it in his

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.340
suit.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:00.499
This could be a joke about the narrative structure
of the film and the way Deadpool plays around

00:18:00.499 --> 00:18:03.120
segwaying between different times and places.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:07.340
Throughout the movie, Deadpool pokes fun at
the superhero genre in general and shows how

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:11.899
self-aware he is, for example, he jokes about
superhero landings and how bad they are for

00:18:11.899 --> 00:18:16.499
your knees; and when he thinks of the pros
and cons of being a superhero, he lists "lucrative

00:18:16.499 --> 00:18:20.259
film deals, both origin stories and larger
ensemble team movies" as a positive.

00:18:20.259 --> 00:18:25.409
Oh, and at the bar when Weasel tells Wade
the Recruiter guy wants to talk to him, he

00:18:25.409 --> 00:18:29.989
adds 'it may further the plot'; and later
when Wade comes up with his alias Deadpool,

00:18:29.989 --> 00:18:32.370
Weasel comments 'that sounds like a fucking
franchise'.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:36.359
And the animated unicorn which shits money
during the closing credits as the producers'

00:18:36.359 --> 00:18:40.129
names appear on the screen is a joke about
them doing very well for themselves out of

00:18:40.129 --> 00:18:41.799
these superhero movies!

00:18:41.799 --> 00:18:45.549
The post-credits scene where Deadpool appears
in his Ferris Bueller-style dressing gown

00:18:45.549 --> 00:18:47.509
and asks "why are you all still here?"

00:18:47.509 --> 00:18:52.659
is a meta-reference to the popularity of post-credits
scenes in comic book movies, especially Marvel

00:18:52.659 --> 00:18:53.659
movies.

00:18:53.659 --> 00:18:56.649
The look of the whole scene owes a lot to
director John Hughes' film Ferris Bueller's

00:18:56.649 --> 00:19:00.539
Day Off, from the layout of the room and its
two doors to the pictures on the wall, and

00:19:00.539 --> 00:19:01.539
the wallpaper.

00:19:01.539 --> 00:19:05.890
And Reynolds even ends the post-credits with
chicka-chicka, from Yello's song 'Oh Yeah',

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:08.120
which also featured in the classic 80s comedy.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:12.679
Ok, guys, what other easter eggs and references
did you spot in Deadpool?

00:19:12.679 --> 00:19:15.059
What was your favourite moment in the movie?

00:19:15.059 --> 00:19:17.210
I can't wait to read your comments below!

